  "contracts": {
    "brazil": "Documented Câmara events JSON; 14-day window, 100 rows/page, at most three pages. Cancellation/deferred/ended rows skipped; missing starts or capped pagination fail visibly. America/Sao_Paulo starts, official event IDs, no inferred TV replay/end times.",
    "california": "Official calendar-export name/start/location query parameters, not visible event prose or malformed ICS. America/Los_Angeles clocks corroborate the dated public event listing. Empty UID and invalid VALUE=DATE in ICS are not silently repaired; generated two-hour ends are ignored.",
    "harmony": "Publisher util formatter requires a 17-digit millisecond watermark. Corrected requests work on all three sites. Four event groups, numeric status, published records and official IDs; Toronto/Bermuda zones for naive clocks, explicit offsets preserved. Stale suspended events are excluded. Bermuda returned a valid empty four-group response.",
    "us_senate": "Contract fixtures follow the public unitedstates/congress client: meeting/cmte_code/date/room/matter and %d-%b-%Y %I:%M %p. Current endpoint returns 403 in collector and browser; root/current nonempty payload is not independently verified. Empty sentinel recognized conservatively.",
    "new_york": "Publisher-owned Drupal view confirms ICS path, UID=nid, summary=title, date range, location and official node URL. Current endpoint returns 403; current body/date precision is not verified. Strict timed subset accepts explicit UTC or America/New_York/US/Eastern, unfolds lines, rejects floating/DST-ambiguous/recurring records, preserves UID. Date-only-only response is a precision hold, not midnight programmes."
